  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Feed-Forward Network** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(x, w1, b1, w2, b2):\n    x=np.asarray(x,dtype=float); w1=np.asarray(w1,dtype=float); b1=np.asarray(b1,dtype=float); w2=np.asarray(w2,dtype=float); b2=np.asarray(b2,dtype=float)\n    h=x@w1+b1\n    h=np.maximum(h,0) # ReLU in this educational FFN contract\n    return (h@w2+b2).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
